From 1bb5a254a13b935e0f50b6ca757aa7d4ab220ab1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Micheal Waltz <micheal@ecliptik.com>
Date: Wed, 8 Jul 2026 15:44:02 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] dos: patch 0119 -- flush also quiesces the Lever-3 Pixtone
 IRQ-mix source (+ probe)

Task #17 (rc3/rc4 PicoGUS-SB cave-transition screech). Latent-bug fix to the
SDL/0092 silence-flush: it advertised "hard-silence the physical audio path" but
did NOT actually silence it when a Pixtone SFX was active.

Why DOS needs this: SDL_DOSAudioFlushRingSilence zeroes the software ring + the
physical DMA double-buffer + collapses the cursors -- but it left the Lever-3
Pixtone IRQ-mix source running. PixtoneISRMix (in SoundBlasterIRQHandler) walks
g_dos_pix_chan[] and adds active Pixtone SFX PCM DIRECTLY into the DMA buffer on
EVERY ISR fire, AFTER the ring-copy/underrun-silence branch -- bypassing the ring
entirely. So after the flush, the next IRQ re-injected the still-active door /
transition SFX into the DMA buffer; when a load_stage sub-loader (flushSheets /
load_map) then starved the ISR, the SB16 auto-init DMA looped that re-injected
fragment = the screech. The flush zeroing the buffer was defeated one IRQ later.
This is code-confirmed (SoundBlasterIRQHandler PixtoneISRMix call; the flush not
touching g_dos_pix_chan[]) and unifies the intermittency (screech iff a Pixtone
SFX was active at the transition).

Fix: in SDL_DOSAudioFlushRingSilence, under the SAME DOS_DisableInterrupts block
that collapses the cursors, deactivate every g_dos_pix_chan[] (active=false,
channel_id=-1) and zero g_dos_pixtone_active_count -- so PixtoneISRMix injects
nothing after the flush and a starved ISR loops the zeroed buffer (= silence).
UNCONDITIONAL (no separate SDL killswitch): the rc5 A/B toggles the nx-side call
gate SDL_HINT_DOSKUTSU_LOADSTAGE_SILENCE (whether the load_stage flush fires),
not this. Benign at the shared cold-render (nx 0206/0209) call sites too -- a
scene reset should stop SFX anyway. Banner label genericized "pre-cold-render
quiesce" -> "ring+DMA silence quiesce"; the flush banner now prints
pixtone_quiesced=N.

Probe (rides along; zero hot-path cost): SDL_DOSAudioIsrRingWrite() exposes the
software-ring producer byte cursor for the engine's per-cave [loadband-stat]
line (SDL_HINT_DOSKUTSU_LOADBAND_STAT, engine-gated). The other two STAT counters
-- doskutsu_audio_irq_count (fires) and g_dos_pixtone_active_count (the screech
discriminator, the path the ring cursor is blind to) -- are already extern
globals, read directly. No new SDL env var.

g2k confirm (rc5): fix-ON (LOADSTAGE_SILENCE=1) SFX-active transition ->
pixtone_quiesced>0 + pix_active_entry==0 + screech gone; fix-OFF -> pix_active>0
+ screech. Real-HW witness ([[dosbox_not_proxy]]).

Workspace-local patch; not upstreamed (sdl_ai_policy).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Code <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 include/SDL3/SDL_dosaudio_pump.h | 30 +++++++++++++++++++++++
 src/audio/dos/SDL_dosaudio_sb.c  | 42 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++---
 2 files changed, 69 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/include/SDL3/SDL_dosaudio_pump.h b/include/SDL3/SDL_dosaudio_pump.h
index 44ead6553..a176fb217 100644
--- a/include/SDL3/SDL_dosaudio_pump.h
+++ b/include/SDL3/SDL_dosaudio_pump.h
@@ -404,6 +404,36 @@ extern SDL_DECLSPEC int SDLCALL SDL_DOSAudioFlushRingSilence(void);
  */
 extern SDL_DECLSPEC int SDLCALL SDL_DOSAudioPhysicalCapacityFrames(void);
 
+/*
+ * DOSKUTSU patch (SDL/0119, task #17): load-band audio-starvation probe
+ * accessors. Workspace-local; never upstreamed.
+ *
+ * The engine snapshots the load-band counters at load_stage entry (AFTER
+ * SDL_DOSAudioFlushRingSilence) and exit -- gated engine-side by
+ * SDL_HINT_DOSKUTSU_LOADBAND_STAT -- and emits one per-cave [loadband-stat] line
+ * to disambiguate the rc3/rc4 PicoGUS-SB cave-transition screech (whether stale
+ * audio is looping because a post-flush RING write, an active Pixtone IRQ-mix
+ * channel, or an IRQ-starved DMA replay). The other two STAT counters are read
+ * directly from their existing extern globals: doskutsu_audio_irq_count (fires)
+ * and g_dos_pixtone_active_count (active Pixtone IRQ-mix channels -- THE screech
+ * discriminator, exported in SDL3/SDL_dospixtone.h).
+ */
+
+/**
+ * Cumulative software-ring PRODUCER (enqueue) cursor, in BYTES. Frames =
+ * value / bytes-per-frame (1 on the 8-bit U8-mono path). A positive delta
+ * across a load_stage band means the mixer wrote NEW samples into the ring
+ * AFTER the entry-flush (a ring-path post-flush write). NOTE: this is BLIND to
+ * the Lever-3 Pixtone IRQ-mix, which writes the DMA buffer directly (bypassing
+ * the ring) -- use the g_dos_pixtone_active_count global (SDL_dospixtone.h) for
+ * that path.
+ *
+ * \returns the monotonic producer byte cursor (0 when no device is open).
+ * \threadsafety Aligned 32-bit read; safe from the engine main thread.
+ * \since doskutsu workspace-local patch, task #17.
+ */
+extern SDL_DECLSPEC int SDLCALL SDL_DOSAudioIsrRingWrite(void);
+
 #ifdef __cplusplus
 }
 #endif
diff --git a/src/audio/dos/SDL_dosaudio_sb.c b/src/audio/dos/SDL_dosaudio_sb.c
index 00e091b9f..68a96e940 100644
--- a/src/audio/dos/SDL_dosaudio_sb.c
+++ b/src/audio/dos/SDL_dosaudio_sb.c
@@ -1091,12 +1091,33 @@ int SDL_DOSAudioFlushRingSilence(void)
      * the frozen producer write position so avail == 0 -> the ISR takes its
      * underrun-silence memset path. Mirror into the hidden producer cursors so
      * the audio thread's own bookkeeping stays coherent when it resumes. */
+    int pix_quiesced = 0;
     DOS_DisableInterrupts();
     isr_ring_read = isr_ring_write;
     if (hidden) {
         hidden->ring_read = isr_ring_write;
         hidden->ring_write = isr_ring_write;
     }
+    /* DOSKUTSU patch (SDL/0119, task #17): quiesce the Lever-3 Pixtone IRQ-mix
+       source too -- a LATENT-BUG FIX so this "hard-silence" primitive finally
+       delivers true physical silence. Zeroing the ring + DMA above does NOT
+       silence the path when a Pixtone SFX is active: PixtoneISRMix (in
+       SoundBlasterIRQHandler) re-injects the still-active g_dos_pix_chan[]
+       straight into the DMA buffer on the NEXT ISR fire -- so during a load_stage
+       block a starved ISR loops that re-injected SFX = the rc3/rc4 cave-transition
+       screech. Deactivating the channels here (same cli, atomic vs the ISR) closes
+       that hole. UNCONDITIONAL (no separate SDL gate): the rc5 A/B toggles the
+       nx-side call gate SDL_HINT_DOSKUTSU_LOADSTAGE_SILENCE (whether the load_stage
+       flush fires at all), not this. Benign at the cold-render (nx 0206/0209) call
+       sites too -- a scene reset should stop SFX. */
+    for (int c = 0; c < DOS_PIXTONE_CHANNELS; ++c) {
+        if (g_dos_pix_chan[c].active) {
+            g_dos_pix_chan[c].active = false;
+            g_dos_pix_chan[c].channel_id = -1;
+            pix_quiesced++;
+        }
+    }
+    g_dos_pixtone_active_count = 0;
     DOS_EnableInterrupts();
 
     const int ring_frames = isr_ring_size / bpf;
@@ -1104,14 +1125,29 @@ int SDL_DOSAudioFlushRingSilence(void)
     const int total_frames = ring_frames + dma_frames;
     doskutsu_dbg_log("audio: SDL/0092 FlushRingSilence -- ring+DMA zeroed "
                      "(silence_frames_flushed=%d = ring_frames=%d + "
-                     "dma_frames=%d; ring_bytes=%d dma_bytes=%d) "
-                     "pre-cold-render quiesce",
+                     "dma_frames=%d; ring_bytes=%d dma_bytes=%d; "
+                     "pixtone_quiesced=%d) ring+DMA silence quiesce",
                      total_frames, ring_frames, dma_frames,
-                     isr_ring_size, isr_dma_halfdma * 2);
+                     isr_ring_size, isr_dma_halfdma * 2, pix_quiesced);
     /* Nonzero == both buffers fully zeroed (== PhysicalCapacityFrames()). */
     return total_frames;
 }
 
+/* DOSKUTSU patch (SDL/0119, task #17): load-band audio-starvation probe
+   accessor for the software-ring producer cursor. The engine snapshots this at
+   load_stage entry (POST-flush) + exit (gated by SDL_HINT_DOSKUTSU_LOADBAND_STAT
+   engine-side) for the per-cave [loadband-stat] line: a delta > 0 across the band
+   means the mixer wrote new SFX into the RING after the flush. (The OTHER two STAT
+   counters are read directly: doskutsu_audio_irq_count + g_dos_pixtone_active_count
+   are already extern -- see SDL_dos_audio_synth.h / the public SDL_dospixtone.h;
+   g_dos_pixtone_active_count is THE screech discriminator, the path this ring
+   cursor is blind to.) Plain aligned read of already-maintained state -> zero
+   hot-path cost; no SDL-side gate (the engine gates the snapshot/emit). */
+int SDL_DOSAudioIsrRingWrite(void)
+{
+    return isr_ring_write;
+}
+
 /* DOSKUTSU patch (SDL/0092): true total physical silence-flush capacity, in
  * frames. This is the denominator for the flush-instr witness
  * silence_frames_flushed >= ring_capacity_frames: the FULL physical depth that
-- 
2.47.3

